<%= render "layouts/notice", notice: notice %>

<% content_for :title, "Suggested merges" %>

<h1>Suggested merges</h1>

<%= index_actions back: counterparties_path do %>
  <%# The only thing on this screen that asks the API. Everything else, including coming back here after a
      merge, reads the answer already given. %>
  <%= link_to "Suggest again", merge_suggestions_path(refresh: 1), class: "pure-button" %>
<% end %>

<p>
  Sets of names that look like one payee, worked out from the names themselves and the categories you file
  them under. <strong>These are proposals, not decisions</strong> — nothing has been merged. Open one to see
  what would move, change the name if you want a different one, and confirm it there.
</p>

<% if @kept_at %>
  <p>
    Worked out <%= time_ago_in_words(@kept_at) %> ago and kept since, so merging one of these and coming
    back costs nothing. A group you have merged drops off the list. Press
    <strong>Suggest again</strong> for a fresh answer.
  </p>
<% end %>

<p>
  Only the payee names and their category names were sent away to work this out. No amounts, no dates, no
  account numbers and nothing about individual transactions ever leave this machine.
</p>

<% if @error.present? %>
  <p class="row-error"><%= @error %></p>
<% end %>

<% if @groups.any? %>
  <table class="pure-table pure-table-bordered">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Suggested name</th>
        <th>Names it would fold together</th>
        <th>Why</th>
        <th>Categories</th>
        <th></th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <% @groups.each do |group| %>
        <tr>
          <td><%= group.name %></td>
          <td>
            <% group.counterparties.each do |counterparty| %>
              <div><%= link_to counterparty.name, counterparty %></div>
            <% end %>
          </td>
          <td><%= group.reason %></td>
          <td>
            <%# The one signal that a group is wrong which does not need a human to spot it, so it is said
                here rather than left for the confirmation screen. Amber, not red: the merge is allowed and
                may well be right — petrol and groceries from one shop legitimately span two categories. %>
            <% if group.categories_clash? %>
              <span class="row-question" title="These names are filed under more than one category, which often means they are not one payee">
                <%= group.categories.join(", ") %>
              </span>
            <% else %>
              <%= group.categories.join(", ").presence || "—" %>
            <% end %>
          </td>
          <td>
            <%# `from` is what sends the confirmation back here rather than to the counterparties list:
                the same screen is also reached by ticking boxes there, and each way in should lead out
                the way it came. %>
            <%= link_to "Review",
                        new_counterparty_merge_path(ids: group.ids, name: group.name, from: "suggestions"),
                        class: "pure-button" %>
          </td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
<% elsif @error.blank? %>
  <p>
    Nothing to suggest — the names you have look like distinct payees. That is the expected answer on a
    tidy list, and on a short one: there is nothing to compare until you have a few counterparties.
  </p>
<% end %>
